f-11ec-bd6a-cb9fb7963c97/file-1l1tj46el.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l1tj46ek/689ab5f9-9b31-4529-8d3e-afdbb16c8833/51cee1d0-b8ef-11ec-bd6a-cb9fb7963c97/file-1l1tj46el.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l1tj46ek/689ab5f9-9b31-4529-8d3e-afdbb16c8833/51cee1d0-b8ef-11ec-bd6a-cb9fb7963c97/file-1l1tj46el.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>The number of unpaired electrons is P = 5, Q = 3 and R = 4. From the relation <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.639ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"15.061ex\" height=\"2.851ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -977.5 6657 1260\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D707\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D707\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(880.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msqrt\" transform=\"translate(1936.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(0,67.5)\"><use data-c=\"221A\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-SO-221A\"></use></g><g transform=\"translate(1020,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(600,0)\"><use data-c=\"28\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-28\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(989,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1811.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(2811.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(3311.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-29\"></use></g></g><rect width=\"3700.4\" height=\"60\" x=\"1020\" y=\"857.5\"></rect></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, where n is the number of unpaired electrons, we have the order of spin only magnetic moment as Q &lt; R &lt; P.</p>"}]}